%!TEX root = notes.tex
When possible, all BibTeX entries should come from MathSciNet:
https://mathscinet.ams.org/
Click the "Cite" button. (As Advised by Dr. Philip Hackney)

The citation key should typically be in the form AuthorNames:XYZ where XYZ is an abbreviation of the title of the work. (As Advised by Dr. Philip Hackney)
Separate sections are provided below for books / papers / preprints / web, and within each section entries should be alphabetized by last name.

I(Durga) have been using Zotero an windows software to store the articles and books that you are studing or following. It provides a great way to get the citation.

For the prople who use TexStudio: you have to first run the .bib file and then run the main file to get the citation in the notes.
For the people who use VSCode:  You don't need any extra step to get the citaton correct. It works smoothly there.
For other softwares I(Durga) have no idea.


